WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.364
openRocode

00:00:01.553 --> 00:00:02.838
an open harness

00:00:03.366 --> 00:00:04.509
Works with Claude

00:00:04.557 --> 00:00:05.972
GPT or any

00:00:05.783 --> 00:00:07.446
OpenAI-compatible model

00:00:07.585 --> 00:00:09.094
I built openRocode

00:00:09.118 --> 00:00:10.167
the open harness

00:00:09.979 --> 00:00:11.629
for LLM-driven robots

00:00:11.712 --> 00:00:13.009
so LLM can

00:00:12.821 --> 00:00:13.929
drive robots

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:15.719
A dashboard shows

00:00:15.614 --> 00:00:16.439
each step with

00:00:16.251 --> 00:00:17.135
the model's own

00:00:16.946 --> 00:00:18.161
words code and

00:00:17.972 --> 00:00:18.668
pictures

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:19.352
so you can

00:00:19.163 --> 00:00:20.189
watch and steer

00:00:20.001 --> 00:00:20.613
a run

00:00:21.134 --> 00:00:22.431
One sentence in

00:00:22.514 --> 00:00:23.527
the model writes

00:00:23.339 --> 00:00:23.881
code

00:00:24.094 --> 00:00:25.249
the harness runs

00:00:25.061 --> 00:00:25.957
it as guarded

00:00:25.768 --> 00:00:27.277
motion and records

00:00:27.136 --> 00:00:28.079
every step

00:00:28.218 --> 00:00:29.043
Watch it in

00:00:28.855 --> 00:00:29.751
full quality

00:00:29.893 --> 00:00:31.284
openRocode is an

00:00:31.108 --> 00:00:32.381
open agent harness

00:00:32.192 --> 00:00:33.336
that turns robot

00:00:33.148 --> 00:00:34.645
control into 3D

00:00:34.457 --> 00:00:35.517
computer use

00:00:36.054 --> 00:00:37.068
Full story on

00:00:36.879 --> 00:00:37.775
the dashboard
